- Editor of one value of a `view.tree` property, dispatching on the shape of the
- value and recursing into composite ones. Port of the value editor of studio and
- its six sub editors, plus a seventh the studio has no equivalent of: the wire `=`
- of section 1. Deviations are marked at their place.
-
- Every class here derives from something OUTSIDE this file, and that is a rule,
- not a coincidence. Declarations of a `view.tree` are emitted before the
- handwritten bodies of the same module, so a class inheriting a neighbour from
- this very file would extend the version without its `.view.ts` methods — half
- the behaviour gone, nothing reported. Studio can chain its object editor onto its
- dictionary editor because there the two live in separate modules. List,
- dictionary and object are therefore one class with two flags rather than three
- classes in a chain.
- @see ../../../../ARCHITECTURE.md section 3
$bog_vmap_app_inspect_value $mol_view
	- Writing serializes the node back into the document.
	tree? $mol_tree2_empty
	- Offered as binding targets.
	binds /string
	- Nodes a wire may start from, by name, each carrying the class it is declared
	- with and the ports that class has. Both ends of a wire are picked out of this
	- one map, so neither end can be spelled by hand into something that does not
	- exist.
	nodes *
	- A refusal has to be legible, and on its own it is not: the string field of mol
	- catches what a setter throws and puts the message into `setCustomValidity`,
	- which the browser shows on form submit and nowhere else. In a form that is
	- never submitted the value silently stays out of the document and the field
	- keeps the text nobody accepted — the document is safe and the person is lost.
	alarm? \
	sub <= editors /$mol_view
	Alarm $mol_view sub / <= alarm
	- Every editor is declared, one is rendered. Studio picks the same way and then
	- copies the context onto the chosen instance field by field. Here the context
	- arrives through ordinary bindings instead, so the wiring is visible in the
	- declaration and type checked, and swapping the shape of a value cannot leave
	- an editor holding a stale accessor.
	String $bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_string
		tree? <=> tree?
	Number $bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_number
		tree? <=> tree?
		alarm? <=> alarm?
	Bool $bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_bool
		tree? <=> tree?
	Seq $bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_seq
		tree? <=> tree?
		keyed <= seq_keyed false
		klass <= seq_klass false
		binds <= binds
		nodes <= nodes
		alarm? <=> alarm?
	Bind $bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_bind
		tree? <=> tree?
		binds <= binds
		nodes <= nodes
		alarm? <=> alarm?
	Wire $bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_wire
		tree? <=> tree?
		nodes <= nodes
		alarm? <=> alarm?
	Raw $bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_raw
		tree? <=> tree?

- Multi line text field. The text area of mol, which studio uses here, is a code
- editor with a gutter and a highlighter; the plain string field is an `<input>`,
- which cannot hold a newline, so a two line value would collapse to one line on
- the first keystroke, silently. The `<textarea>` in between is neither, and is the
- shape this needs.
$bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_area $mol_string
	dom_name \textarea
	attr *
		^
		rows <= rows 1
	- The string field binds Enter to `submit`. In an input that is the only
	- sensible meaning of the key; in a text area it is the one key that has to
	- reach the field itself.
	plugins /

- A text value: `\Текст`, or `@ \Текст` when it goes through the locale table.
$bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_string $mol_view
	tree? $mol_tree2_empty
	sub /
		<= Text $bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_area
			hint \текст
			rows <= text_rows 1
			value? <=> text? \
		<= Locale $mol_check
			title \@
			hint \Многоязычное: текст уедет в таблицу локалей
			checked? <=> locale? false

