- A value with no editor of its own: `null`, `^`, or a shape this module has no
- form for. Shown as its own source text and left alone, because failing here
- would take out the whole property list over one node nobody was editing.
$bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_raw $mol_view
	tree? $mol_tree2_empty
	sub / <= raw \

- A list `/`, a dictionary `*` or an object `$Класс`: a column of value editors
- with an add button. The three differ in two bits — whether an element carries a
- key, and whether the node itself carries a class name — and in nothing else.
$bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_seq $mol_view
	tree? $mol_tree2_empty
	binds /string
	nodes *
	alarm? \
	- Elements are `ключ значение` pairs rather than bare values: a dictionary and
	- an object, not a list.
	keyed false
	- The node type is the name of a class and is editable: an object.
	klass false
	sub <= seq_sub /$mol_view
	Class_name $mol_string
		hint \класс
		value? <=> class_name? \
	Items $mol_view
		sub <= items /
	Add $mol_button_minor
		title <= add_title \
		hint \Добавить
		click? <=> item_add? null
	- A row of the sequence is a class of its own because it has to be: a named
	- sub view declared inside a keyed one is hoisted by `upper` into a property of
	- the root WITHOUT the key, so every row would share one editor.
	Item* $bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_item
		keyed <= keyed
		marker <= item_marker* false
		key? <=> item_key*? \
		value? <=> item_value*? $mol_tree2_empty
		binds <= binds
		nodes <= nodes
		drop? <=> item_drop*? null

- One element of a list, or one entry of a dictionary when it carries a key.
$bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_item $mol_view
	value? $mol_tree2_empty
