		hint \Убрать
		click? <=> drop?

- A binding: `<= prop`, `<=> prop` or `=> prop`, optionally carrying a default.
-
- The target is one bare token and there is nowhere to put a second one, which is
- the guard against the middle form of `<=`: `<= Calc result` looks like a wire,
- is not one, and either kills the build with a message about default values or
- ships `Calc(){ return result }` into the bundle.
$bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_bind $mol_view
	tree? $mol_tree2_empty
	binds /string
	nodes *
	alarm? \
	sub <= bind_sub /$mol_view
	Op $mol_view sub / <= op \
	- Picked, like both ends of a wire. One end of a link chosen from a list and the
	- other typed by hand would read as an inconsistency of the editor rather than a
	- difference between the two things.
	Target $mol_select
		hint \свойство
		value? <=> target? \
		options <= binds
	Default $bog_vmap_app_inspect_value
		tree? <=> default_value? $mol_tree2_empty
		binds <= binds
		nodes <= nodes

- A wire: `= Узел порт`, the two token form of section 1.
-
- Both ends are PICKED, not typed: the node out of the nodes the document declares,
- the port out of the ports that node's class has. A wire that cannot be spelled
- wrong needs no message about being spelled wrong.
-
- The checks stay underneath all the same, because the pickers are an interface and
- the document is not: both ends still go through the token guard of the language
- module, so a sign or a space cannot be smuggled inside one, and the node is still
- checked against the declared list. The `?` of a two way wire lives on the property
- signature and is moved by the row, through `wire_add`, so that both ends always
- move together.
$bog_vmap_app_inspect_value_wire $mol_view
	tree? $mol_tree2_empty
	nodes *
	alarm? \
	sub <= wire_sub /$mol_view
	Row $mol_view
		sub <= wire_row /$mol_view
	- The operator, shown for the same reason the binding shows `<=`: a wire and a
	- binding are two different things and the difference is one glyph.
	Op $mol_view sub / \=
	Origin $mol_select
		hint \узел
		value? <=> origin? \
		options <= node_names /string
	Dot $mol_view sub / \.
	Port_pick $mol_select
		hint \порт
		value? <=> port? \
		options <= ports /string
	- Free text is the fallback and never the default: it is offered exactly when
	- there is no list to pick from, that is when the pack does not carry the class
	- of the node. Refusing to edit at all would be the wrong answer — a document
	- may legitimately name a class the loaded pack has never heard of.
	Port_free $mol_string
		hint \порт
		value? <=> port? \
	- Rendered only when there is something to say.
	Note $mol_view sub / <= note \
